.TH USBRADIOPLUS-TUNE 8 "August 2026" "USBRadioPlus alpha" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
usbradioplus-tune \- tune and monitor a USBRadioPlus radio interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usbradioplus-tune
.br
.B usbradioplus-tune
[-n node] [--check] [--offline] [--config path] [--lock path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This utility configures USBRadioPlus from a keyboard-operated terminal.
Run it as root on the Asterisk node. Processing edits are written and applied
immediately. Live calibration values are retained by the explicit save action.
.PP
Menu buttons use consistent action names. Select opens the highlighted item,
Apply commits an edit, Back returns one menu level, Exit leaves the utility,
Cancel abandons an edit, and Close dismisses information without changing it.
The main menu operates on the active RadioPlus device. It provides:
.TP
.B Select active USB device
Choose one configured radio interface. Swap exchanges USB assignments between
two configured interfaces; it does not exchange their radio settings.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX noise level
With no carrier present, adjust USB capture level and the DSP carrier-squelch
starting point. Flat discriminator calibration targets 27,000 peak PCM codes,
accepts values within 2,750 codes, and makes at most 12 attempts. Each attempt
reports peak and RMS levels in PCM codes and dBFS. This requires flat
discriminator audio and should be followed by receiver-level and squelch
verification.
.TP
.B Set RX voice level using display
Show a live deviation bar, then accept a 0--999 receive voice setting. This
adjusts the local processing input gain. Press any key to leave the live
display and reach the setting prompt.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX CTCSS level
Measure received CTCSS and adjust decoder level. Apply a carrier with the
configured tone and specified tone deviation before selecting this action.
.TP
.B Set RX squelch level
Display current DSP signal strength and accept a 0--999 squelch setting. Higher
numbers require a stronger signal to open.
.TP
.B Set TX voice level
Set the 0--999 mixer level for the output carrying voice or composite audio.
When test-tone keying is enabled, the action keys PTT and sends 1 kHz for five
seconds.
.TP
.B Set auxiliary voice level
Set the 0--999 level on the output configured as auxvoice. The action is
unavailable unless one output mixer carries auxvoice.
.TP
.B Set TX CTCSS level
Set CTCSS deviation from 0--999. When test-tone keying is enabled, the action
keys PTT and sends CTCSS for five seconds.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX voice level
Adjust the local processing input gain from a received 1 kHz tone at 3 kHz
deviation. This action requires flat discriminator audio and a steady
calibrated signal.
.TP
.B Echo mode
Select Echo mode in the Local receiver menu to enable or disable it.
Record a received transmission and return it to the transmitter for alignment.
With software duplex-3 local repeat active, echo uses the native 48 kHz receive
and transmit path. Otherwise it uses the 8 kHz Asterisk-path playback. Keying,
maximum duration, and start and stop behavior are the same for both paths.
Disable echo when the test is complete.
.TP
.B Flash transmitter
Send three one-second PTT and 1 kHz tone bursts separated by 1.5 seconds.
.TP
.B Carrier and CTCSS source
Select the COS and tone indication sources supported by usbradioplus.conf(5).
.TP
.B Hardware and processing options
Set receiver audio source, RX-on and TX-off delays, transmit pre-emphasis and
limiting selections, and USB output A and B routing.
It also sets the transmit soft-limiter onset from 5000 through 13000, the
duplex-3 repeat level from 0 through 999, and whether duplex-3 repeat audio uses
the CM119 hardware mixer or the native software path.
.TP
.B Configure audio processing
Each source has a Stages menu for enabling or disabling its processing stages.
Select Processing order there to view or edit the comma-separated order of
equalizer, expander, agc, deesser, compressor, and limiter. Each enabled stage
must appear exactly once; disabled stages may remain in the order. RNNoise,
receiver filters, and final transmitter filters and limiter have fixed positions
and cannot be placed in this list. Apply saves the order; Cancel leaves it unchanged.
The Equalizer menu edits the low shelf,
mid-band bell, and high shelf. The De-esser menu edits its center frequency,
bandwidth, threshold, ratio, maximum reduction, attack, and release.
See
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5)
for option definitions and ranges.
On return, the radio tuning menu refreshes its displayed values.
.TP
.B Print current parameter values
Report the selected interface, USB device, output routing, and principal RX/TX
levels.
.TP
.B Live statistics and status
Display COS, CTCSS, PTT, RX peak/RMS/clipping, and TX peak/RMS/clipping
together. Press Enter to return. TX statistics report that PTT is clear when
the transmitter is idle.
.TP
.B Save current parameter values
Write device selection, signal sources, mixer and radio levels, squelch,
delays, boosts, transmitter processing selections, and limiter setpoint to
usbradioplus.conf. EEPROM values are also written when EEPROM storage is enabled.
.SH CONFIGURATION MENUS
The processing menu selects local receiver, linked audio, or voice and telemetry.
If the configuration file is absent, the utility installs a copy of the shipped
default before opening. Hardware menus provide device selection and swapping,
automatic RX calibration, live RX level adjustment, CTCSS calibration,
service-monitor transmit adjustment, auxiliary-output adjustment, test-tone
keying, transmitter flash, and one continuous combined RX, TX,
COS, CTCSS, and PTT display.
Echo control is in the Local receiver menu.
Only controls applicable to the selected source are shown. Stage toggles use
single keys and the arrow, Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Escape, B, and Q keys. Numeric
pages validate both the documented range and dependent relationships such as a
low-pass cutoff being above its high-pass cutoff.
.PP
The Filters page groups every fixed filter that applies to the selected source.
For local receive it selects or disables CTCSS notch or high-pass
filtering and sets the applicable cutoff or notch width. For voice and telemetry
it enables or disables the transmit brick-wall band-pass and post-limiter
low-pass and sets their cutoff frequencies. Dynamics pages contain the
high-pass and low-pass detector filters for AGC, expansion, and compression.
The Compressor and Limiter pages each select Single band or Three bands.
Single-band mode shows full-band controls; three-band mode shows the low/mid
and mid/high crossovers and independent low-, mid-, and high-band controls.
The default divisions are below 500 Hz, 500 to 2000 Hz, and above 2000 Hz.
The upper crossover must be below half the source sample rate: below 4000 Hz
on an 8 kHz link. Compression detector filters apply only in single-band mode;
three-band compression measures each band's own RMS level. Changing modes
updates the page immediately and keeps inactive settings for later use.
The AGC page also sets detector-band RMS target and averaging, maximum boost
and attenuation, gain-increase and gain-decrease rates, activity threshold
and hysteresis, gain-increase hold, and target deadband. Set either AGC
detector cutoff to 0 to disable that filter. Inactive audio freezes AGC gain
without muting; the hold delays gain increases only. The target is not a peak
or full-band RMS target. See the automatic gain control section of
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5)
for the ranges and detector behavior.
.PP
Each accepted edit is written atomically and reloaded so it can be evaluated
live. If validation or reload fails, the preceding file and active settings are
restored. Save commits the current processing session. Discard restores the
last saved state, including when exiting. A separate action writes current
radio tuning to usbradioplus.conf and, when enabled, the interface EEPROM. The
main menu can also create a timestamped backup.
.TP
.B -n node
Select the active RadioPlus channel before opening either tuning interface.
.TP
.B --check
Validate prerequisites and confirm that the configured local, link, and
voice/telemetry sections can be read and complete shipped defaults are available.
Both plain and gzip-compressed installed sample files are supported.
.TP
.B --offline
With --check, do not require Asterisk or the terminal menu package. This is
intended for installation and package tests.
.TP
.B --config path
Use another USBRadioPlus configuration file.
.TP
.B --lock path
Use another menu lock file.
.SH SERVICE-MONITOR PROCEDURE
Use a dummy load or authorized test frequency. Set capture gain first with an
unmodulated receiver and verify that ADC rail counts remain zero. Apply a
calibrated 1 kHz signal at system deviation and set recovered RX voice level.
Apply the configured CTCSS tone at the specified tone deviation and verify
decode margin.
.PP
Key into a service monitor, set voice peak deviation, then set CTCSS deviation.
Verify peak and RMS level, clipping, occupied bandwidth, PTT operation, and
tone turn-off behavior before saving. Repeat checks after reconnecting USB and
after restarting Asterisk.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf
Named radio channels, hardware settings, saved tuning, and processing graphs.
.TP
.B /run/lock/usbradioplus-tune.lock
Processing-menu single-instance lock.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usbradioplus (7),
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5),
.BR modules.conf (5),
.BR rpt.conf (5)
